{
  "id": "stem-changing-verbs",
  "level": "A1",
  "title": "Verben mit Wechsel des Stammvokals",
  "group": "Verbs",
  "sourceFile": "stemchange.html",
  "overviewSource": "stemchangeexpl.html",
  "overview": {
    "blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Some strong verbs change their stem vowel only in the du and er/sie/es present-tense forms. The wir, ihr, and sie/Sie forms use the infinitive stem."
      },
      {
        "type": "table",
        "content": "",
        "rows": [
          [
            "Change",
            "Infinitive",
            "du",
            "er/sie/es"
          ],
          [
            "e → i",
            "geben",
            "gibst",
            "gibt"
          ],
          [
            "e → ie",
            "sehen",
            "siehst",
            "sieht"
          ],
          [
            "a → ä",
            "fahren",
            "fährst",
            "fährt"
          ],
          [
            "au → äu",
            "laufen",
            "läufst",
            "läuft"
          ]
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": "Normal personal endings are added after the vowel change. Do not change the stem for ich: ich gebe, ich sehe, ich fahre."
      },
      {
        "type": "example",
        "content": "",
        "de": "Du fährst nach Berlin, aber wir fahren nach Hamburg.",
        "note": "du changes a → ä; wir keeps the original stem"
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
